    "text": "{\"anomaly_detected\": true, \"confidence\": 0.6, \"anomalies\": [{\"category\": \"bridged_nets\", \"components\": [\"R60\", \"D30\"], \"pins\": [\"R60.1\", \"R60.2\", \"D30.2\", \"D30.4\"], \"nets\": [\"Net-(D30-K2)\", \"ESTOP_OUT\"], \"observed\": \"R60 connects the cathode K2 of the dual LED D30 to ESTOP_OUT, which is also the anode A2 (D30.4) of the same LED. The LED channel 2 therefore forms a closed loop from ESTOP_OUT back to ESTOP_OUT with no path to ground, so no current can flow and the indicator cannot light. The companion channel is wired correctly: R59 runs from K1 to GND.\", \"expected\": \"The R60 series resistor should return the LED cathode K2 to ground, mirroring R59 on K1, so that the ESTOP_OUT-driven anode A2 can source current through the LED to GND.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"ESTOP_OUT : D30.4(A2,input) J13.6(Pin_6,passive) J2.6(Pin_6,passive) R60.2(passive) U36.4(Y,output)\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"Net-(D30-K2) : D30.2(K2,input) R60.1(passive)\"}, {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"R60 Net-_D30-K2_ ESTOP_OUT 130\"}, {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"R59 Net-_D30-K1_ 0 130\"}], \"impact\": \"The e-stop status LED on channel 2 of D30 never illuminates, so the operator loses a visual e-stop indication. The electrical e-stop path itself is not directly affected.\", \"confidence\": 0.6}, {\"category\": \"wrong_value\", \"components\": [\"R17\", \"R16\", \"U12\"], \"pins\": [\"R17.2\", \"R17.1\", \"R16.2\", \"U12.3\"], \"nets\": [\"+12V\", \"FB\"], \"observed\": \"The TPS61040 feedback divider uses R17 = 1.8M from +12V to FB and R16 = 205k from FB to GND. With the TPS61040's roughly 200 mV feedback reference, this sets the output to about 0.2 \u00d7 (1 + 1.8M/205k) \u2248 2 V, not 12 V.\", \"expected\": \"A divider intended to regulate the +12V rail should have a ratio of about 59:1 (for example R17 near 12M with R16 near 205k) so that the output sits near 12 V.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"R17 | 1.8M | Resistor_SMD:R_0603_1608Metric | Device:R | Resistor | LCSC=C403036\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"FB : C19.2(passive) R16.2(passive) R17.1(passive) U12.3(FB,passive)\"}, {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"R17 FB +12V 1.8Meg\"}], \"impact\": \"If the value is wrong, the +12V rail would regulate near 2 V, starving any 12 V load. This finding is lower confidence because the spec does not state the intended +12V level.\", \"confidence\": 0.25}], \"summary\": \"The strongest anomaly is that R60 is tied to ESTOP_OUT rather than ground, which shorts out the D30 channel-2 LED and prevents its indication, while its channel-1 counterpart R59 returns correctly to ground. A lower-confidence possible wrong value on the +12V boost feedback divider is also noted.\"}",
